quran[14]{c,v,t}:
  21,11,And how many towns engaged in wrongdoing have We demolished and (then) raised other people after them?
  21,12,"So, when they felt Our Might (coming upon them), see how they tried to escape."
  21,13,(The angels said:) ‘Do not try to escape (now)! Return to the pleasures you were given to enjoy and to your dwellings. So that you may be questioned!’
  21,14,"They said: ‘Woe to us! We have, indeed, been wrongdoers!’"
  21,15,"This remained their cry until We made them a cut-off field, extinct (like burnt ashes)."
  21,16,"We did not create the heavens, earth, or whatever is between them just for play."
  21,17,"Had We wished to have some entertainment, We would have indeed found it in Our presence if We were to do (so)."
  21,18,"Rather, We cast truth against falsehood, and it crushes its head. And behold, it (i.e. falsehood) vanishes away. And woe to you for what you allege (about Allah)."
  21,19,"To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and the earth. And those who remain in His presence are neither arrogant to worship Him, nor do they get tired."
  21,20,They glorify (Him) night and day (and) they never take a momentary break.
  21,21,"Have they taken gods from the earth, who raise (the dead) alive?"
  21,22,"Had there been gods in them (i.e. the heavens and the earth) other than Allah, they would surely have collapsed. So, Glory be to Allah, the Lord of the Throne, above what they attribute to Him."
  21,23,"He cannot be questioned about what He does, but they (all) shall be questioned (about their actions)."
  21,24,"Have they taken gods besides Him? Say: ‘Produce your evidence! This is a reminder for those with me and a reminder for those before me.’ Instead, most of them do not know the truth, so they are disregardful."
